---
title: Air Fryer Potatoes
servings: 2
time required: 20 minutes
course: Side Dish
cuisine: American
---

Rinse @potato{3%small}(can use 2 medium or 1 large potato too) with water. If you dislike potato skin, peel your potatoes, but this isn’t needed. Cut potatoes into bite-sized pieces or strips if you prefer french fry style. Put cut potatoes into a bowl with water to soak to remove excess starch. If needed, start preheating #air fryer{} to 400℉ for ~{5-10%minutes}.

Drain water from your potatoes, then coat lightly with @olive oil{} or @melted butter{}. Sprinkle desired seasonings if they can withstand heat and toss, i.e. @seasoned salt{}, @pepper{}, @garlic powder{}, @Italian Seasoning{}.

Put potatoes in air fryer rack, avoiding overcrowding if possible. Air fry for ~{10-15%minutes}, until desired crispiness. Toss potatoes every ~{5%minutes} to ensure even cooking. Add remaining seasonings (i.e. @furikake{}, @shichimi togarashi{}, @hot sauce{}, etc.) as desired by tossing in the same bowl.

> For a fun twist serve with gravy and cheese curds for a quick mock poutine. 